     "description": "A heart-and-soul player for the Flyers, Rick Tocchet began his career in Philadelphia and spent the majority of his 18 NHL seasons embodying the team\u2019s gritty identity. A key figure for the Flyers during the 1980s, Tocchet helped propel the team to two Stanley Cup Final appearances. In the 1987 Stanley Cup Playoffs, Tocchet delivered a defining moment in Game 6 against Montreal, scoring the game-winning goal in the third period on the road to clinch the series and send Philadelphia to the Final.\n\nOfficially Licensed Product of the NHL, NHLPA, and/or NHLAA. All copyright, logos, and marks are the property of their respective owners and are used, under license, by Sweet. All Rights Reserved. [Terms Apply](https://nhlbreakaway.com/terms).",
